    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e933f914-19bc-5eeb-bafa-105fd4ec5181",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $Y$, where\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 16 & -12\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $1$st rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $3$rd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:=(-2)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 16 & -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =Y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:=(-2)\\cdot {R}_{3}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "6794b10c-9282-5950-a758-1556c8a1e516",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "c7e0b0ca-23a6-5350-b55e-5430cab1476d",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{R}_{3}:=(-2)\\cdot {R}_{3}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "53eebc06-1d9c-5011-9575-afd5630912ef",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{R}_{3}:=\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\cdot {R}_{3}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "4b60f6ee-7491-5502-a0c6-79e8b5f947af",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-6)\\cdot {R}_{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "422022fa-05a7-527a-a51d-7f723a7fab6f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2\\cdot {R}_{3}"
