      ":question/id": "4462e0ea-63b4-599a-8f24-57b30976a944",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nW=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 22 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $1$st and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row.\n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 22 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
